body:
Hi, thank you for the PR!

> It is safe to call [zxdg_exporter_v2_export_toplevel()](https://wayland.app/protocols/xdg-foreign-unstable-v2#zxdg_exporter_v2:request:export_toplevel) only after the xdg_surface role ([xdg_toplevel](https://wayland.app/protocols/xdg-shell#xdg_toplevel)) has been confirmed.

The spec nor the error imply this, where did you find this out? All it says is that it needs to be an `xdg_toplevel`, not that it has to be mapped.

On what compositor can you replicate this issue? Maybe it's some compositor-specific quirk.

Additionally, does it happen if the exporter is created after committing the surface but before configuration?

```diff
diff --git a/platform/linuxbsd/wayland/wayland_thread.cpp b/platform/linuxbsd/wayland/wayland_thread.cpp
index 9c149faa37..1daf35ab85 100644
--- a/platform/linuxbsd/wayland/wayland_thread.cpp
+++ b/platform/linuxbsd/wayland/wayland_thread.cpp
@@ -4139,6 +4139,8 @@ void WaylandThread::window_create(DisplayServerEnums::WindowID p_window_id, cons
 	ws.frame_callback = wl_surface_frame(ws.wl_surface);
 	wl_callback_add_listener(ws.frame_callback, &frame_wl_callback_listener, &ws);
 
+	wl_surface_commit(ws.wl_surface);
+
 	if (registry.xdg_exporter_v2) {
 		ws.xdg_exported_v2 = zxdg_exporter_v2_export_toplevel(registry.xdg_exporter_v2, ws.wl_surface);
 		zxdg_exported_v2_add_listener(ws.xdg_exported_v2, &xdg_exported_v2_listener, &ws);
@@ -4146,8 +4148,6 @@ void WaylandThread::window_create(DisplayServerEnums::WindowID p_window_id, cons
 		ws.xdg_exported_v1 = zxdg_exporter_v1_export(registry.xdg_exporter_v1, ws.wl_surface);
 		zxdg_exported_v1_add_listener(ws.xdg_exported_v1, &xdg_exported_v1_listener, &ws);
 	}
-
-	wl_surface_commit(ws.wl_surface);
 }
 
 void WaylandThread::window_create_popup(DisplayServerEnums::WindowID p_window_id, DisplayServerEnums::WindowID p_parent_id, Rect2i p_rect) {
```
(applied on top of `master`)

Thank you! It looks like libdecor is waiting for... something before getting the toplevel.

I wouldn't call it a bug in libdecor; It looks more like it depends on the environment it runs on. We kinda give for granted that we'll have a response right away, which isn't actually guaranteed (see #115739 for example).

After looking at its source code, apparently it's not yet initialized (waits for a callback). Maybe all it takes is to move the libdecor initialization earlier?

```patch
diff --git a/platform/linuxbsd/wayland/wayland_thread.cpp b/platform/linuxbsd/wayland/wayland_thread.cpp
index b15805a4e3..541cd8d7e4 100644
--- a/platform/linuxbsd/wayland/wayland_thread.cpp
+++ b/platform/linuxbsd/wayland/wayland_thread.cpp
@@ -5167,6 +5167,28 @@ Error WaylandThread::init() {
 		wl_display = wl_display_connect(embedder_socket_path.utf8().get_data());
 	}
 
+#ifdef LIBDECOR_ENABLED
+	bool libdecor_found = true;
+
+	bool skip_libdecor = OS::get_singleton()->get_environment("GODOT_WAYLAND_DISABLE_LIBDECOR") == "1";
+
+#ifdef SOWRAP_ENABLED
+	if (!skip_libdecor && initialize_libdecor(dylibloader_verbose) != 0) {
+		libdecor_found = false;
+	}
+#endif // SOWRAP_ENABLED
+
+	if (skip_libdecor) {
+		print_verbose("Skipping libdecor check because GODOT_WAYLAND_DISABLE_LIBDECOR is set to 1.");
+	} else {
+		if (libdecor_found) {
+			libdecor_context = libdecor_new(wl_display, (struct libdecor_interface *)&libdecor_interface);
+		} else {
+			print_verbose("libdecor not found. Client-side decorations disabled.");
+		}
+	}
+#endif // LIBDECOR_ENABLED
+
 	ERR_FAIL_NULL_V_MSG(wl_display, ERR_CANT_CREATE, "Can't connect to a Wayland display.");
 
 	thread_data.wl_display = wl_display;
@@ -5220,28 +5242,6 @@ Error WaylandThread::init() {
 	// TODO: Async?
 	wl_display_roundtrip(wl_display);
 
-#ifdef LIBDECOR_ENABLED
-	bool libdecor_found = true;
-
-	bool skip_libdecor = OS::get_singleton()->get_environment("GODOT_WAYLAND_DISABLE_LIBDECOR") == "1";
-
-#ifdef SOWRAP_ENABLED
-	if (!skip_libdecor && initialize_libdecor(dylibloader_verbose) != 0) {
-		libdecor_found = false;
-	}
-#endif // SOWRAP_ENABLED
-
-	if (skip_libdecor) {
-		print_verbose("Skipping libdecor check because GODOT_WAYLAND_DISABLE_LIBDECOR is set to 1.");
-	} else {
-		if (libdecor_found) {
-			libdecor_context = libdecor_new(wl_display, (struct libdecor_interface *)&libdecor_interface);
-		} else {
-			print_verbose("libdecor not found. Client-side decorations disabled.");
-		}
-	}
-#endif // LIBDECOR_ENABLED
-
 	cursor_theme_name = OS::get_singleton()->get_environment("XCURSOR_THEME");
 
 	unscaled_cursor_size = OS::get_singleton()->get_environment("XCURSOR_SIZE").to_int();
```
(on top of `master`)

That should give it ample time to initialize alongside us.
